  "body": "## What changed\n\n- A new file, `crates/motion/src/machining2d/contour_whole_reach.rs`, holds `reach_up` and `band_sweep`. When a ring of a deeper band has a tool sweep that reaches outside every sweep cut so far, `reach_up` adds every flat level under Top Z above the ring's first level. Each pass is then at most one stepdown under the pass before it on that ring.\n- If the ring cannot be proven clear of the part at the added levels, the operation is refused by name. The toolpath is not made, so nothing posts.\n- A ring whose sweep stays inside the cut sweeps is not changed (an outline that does not grow).\n- A level at Top Z is never added, because it removes no material.\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/contour_whole.rs` keeps the union of the band sweeps (`cover`) and calls `reach_up` after `check_unread`.\n- Decision entry: `docs/decisions/2597-new-outline-from-top-z.md`. The stepdown is the axial limit of the operation. So there is no new parameter: its other value would post the buried pass again.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Before the fix, on the #2597 part (boss 30x30 to Z25 on a 60x60 base to Z10, D10, stepdown 5): the base ring was first cut at Z5, 20.000 mm under Top Z 25 (levels `[5.0, 0.0]`).\n- Before the fix, on a three-step part: the middle ring was first cut at Z18, 12.000 mm under Top Z 30.\n- After the fix: each ring steps down from Top Z in steps of at most the stepdown, and ends at its floor. The depth verifier gives no warning.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `camcraft-motion` `contour_whole_new_outline`:\n  - `new_larger_outline_below_top_z_steps_down_from_top_z`\n  - `every_new_outline_of_three_steps_steps_down_from_top_z`\n  - `an_outline_that_does_not_grow_is_not_walked_again_above`\n\n  The first two fail on main and pass with the fix.\n- `camcraft-motion` `contour_whole`: `earlier_blind_hole_stop_does_not_hide_later_counterbore_change` has a changed pin. The upper bore now also has a lap at extent 7 at Z16 and Z12. This is correct: the stock core inside the upper bore grows there. The new helper `assert_bore_laps_at` checks one full lap for each extent and no other move in the bore. All 8 tests pass.\n- `camcraft-app` `contour_whole_step`: all 3 tests pass. `case1` caught a `Crossing` warning in the first version, when a level at Top Z was added. The fix leaves out the Top Z level.\n- Quick gate `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 121 steps, 0 failed, 26.8 min.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Parts with stock that is narrower than the part's outline. The added passes cut air there (see #2658).\n- Tabs on an added level of a new outline. The tab code was not changed.\n- A run in the GUI and a real post on a machine.\n\n## Goldens\n\nNo CL or NC golden changed. No snapshot PNG changed.\n\n## Shared files\n\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/contour_whole.rs` is also touched by #2538. This PR does not change `contour_depth.rs`.\n- This PR does not touch `tab_bridge.rs` or `contour.rs` (#2561).\n\n## Follow-up\n\n- #2658: start a new outline where the stock starts, not at Top Z.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation).\n\nChangelog: Whole-model 2D Contour: a new, larger outline below Top Z is now cut from Top Z down in steps no deeper than the stepdown, or the operation is refused by name. Before, its first pass buried the tool and posted with no warning.\n\nFixes #2597\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
